  (#("Students as Language Designers" 0 30 (pdf-text-emph bold)) 0.1561 0.43227 0.08551 0.09827 0.09827 0.01277 0.00502 0.2548 0.0748 "SZPSMQ+NimbusRomNo9L-Medi" 0.0142 t nil 3 "SZPSMQ+NimbusRomNo9L-Medi" t)
  ("Computer science enables creation without respect for institutions, and scripting languages are one of" 0.12095 0.90421 0.10735 0.11893 0.11893 0.01158 0.00759 0.2311 0.0733 "WSWLVM+NimbusRomNo9L-Regu" 0.0130 nil nil 13 "WSWLVM+NimbusRomNo9L-Regu" nil)
  ("its best and worst manifestations of this power. I tell students that many of them will go on to design" 0.12095 0.90421 0.12344 0.13503 0.13503 0.01158 0.00711 0.2824 0.0173 "WSWLVM+NimbusRomNo9L-Regu" 0.0130 nil nil 19 "WSWLVM+NimbusRomNo9L-Regu" nil)
  ("programming languages: not large, industrial languages like Java, but small, scripting or domain-specific" 0.12095 0.90421 0.13954 0.15112 0.15112 0.01158 0.0059 0.2830 0.0998 "WSWLVM+NimbusRomNo9L-Regu" 0.0130 nil nil 12 "WSWLVM+NimbusRomNo9L-Regu" nil)
  ("languages that will enhance their productivity. A good example is XACML, a language for separating the" 0.12095 0.90421 0.15563 0.16721 0.16665 0.01158 0.00594 0.2746 0.0733 "WSWLVM+NimbusRomNo9L-Regu" 0.0130 nil nil 15 "WSWLVM+NimbusRomNo9L-Regu" nil)
  ("access-control logic from the rest of the program, using rules with domain-specific combinators. These" 0.12095 0.90421 0.17172 0.18331 0.18331 0.01158 0.00685 0.2710 0.1048 "WSWLVM+NimbusRomNo9L-Regu" 0.0130 nil nil 13 "WSWLVM+NimbusRomNo9L-Regu" nil)
  ("students must therefore learn: (a) to recognize a scope for a domain-specific language, (b) the building-" 0.12095 0.90421 0.18782 0.1994 0.1994 0.01158 0.0064 0.2351 0.0601 "WSWLVM+NimbusRomNo9L-Regu" 0.0130 nil nil 15 "WSWLVM+NimbusRomNo9L-Regu" nil)
  ("blocks that go into most languages, and (c) to avoid the mistakes of past language designers. This vision" 0.12095 0.90421 0.20391 0.21549 0.21549 0.01158 0.00577 0.2576 0.0478 "WSWLVM+NimbusRomNo9L-Regu" 0.0130 nil nil 17 "WSWLVM+NimbusRomNo9L-Regu" nil)
  ("guides the book and my course." 0.12095 0.35305 0.22 0.23159 0.23159 0.01158 0.00458 0.2766 0.0478 "WSWLVM+NimbusRomNo9L-Regu" 0.0130 nil nil 5 "WSWLVM+NimbusRomNo9L-Regu" nil)
