  (#("Teaching the Other 90%" 0 22 (pdf-text-emph bold)) 0.1561 0.36679 0.24965 0.26242 0.26242 0.01277 0.00502 0.2878 0.0774 "SZPSMQ+NimbusRomNo9L-Medi" 0.0142 t nil 3 "SZPSMQ+NimbusRomNo9L-Medi" t)
  ("The textbook realm seems to be split between those that are rich in mathematical rigor but low on" 0.12095 0.90421 0.27149 0.28307 0.28307 0.01158 0.00859 0.2676 0.0285 "WSWLVM+NimbusRomNo9L-Regu" 0.0130 nil nil 17 "WSWLVM+NimbusRomNo9L-Regu" nil)
  ("accessibility, and those high on accessibility but lacking rigor (and, often, even wrong). This puts professors" 0.12095 0.90421 0.28758 0.29917 0.29917 0.01158 0.00405 0.2914 0.0940 "WSWLVM+NimbusRomNo9L-Regu" 0.0130 nil nil 15 "WSWLVM+NimbusRomNo9L-Regu" nil)
  (#("in an unfortunate bind. I believe programming language design should be viewed as a popular activity, in" 84 92 (pdf-text-emph italic)) 0.12095 0.90421 0.30368 0.31526 0.31526 0.01158 0.00533 0.2732 0.0143 "WSWLVM+NimbusRomNo9L-Regu" 0.0130 nil nil 16 "WSWLVM+NimbusRomNo9L-Regu" nil)
  (#("the sense of one that every student must study. This is not because I believe every student should design" 92 99 (pdf-text-emph italic)) 0.12095 0.90421 0.31977 0.33136 0.33136 0.01158 0.00586 0.2315 0.0224 "WSWLVM+NimbusRomNo9L-Regu" 0.0130 nil nil 18 "WSWLVM+NimbusRomNo9L-Regu" nil)
  (#("languages, but because any student might. The student driven away by excessive mathematical rigor is," 35 40 (pdf-text-emph italic)) 0.12095 0.90421 0.33586 0.34745 0.34745 0.01158 0.00674 0.2496 0.0779 "WSWLVM+NimbusRomNo9L-Regu" 0.0130 nil nil 14 "WSWLVM+NimbusRomNo9L-Regu" nil)
  ("sadly, not necessarily going to refrain from creating his own language and inflicting it on the world. The" 0.12095 0.90421 0.35196 0.36354 0.36354 0.01158 0.00583 0.2680 0.0421 "WSWLVM+NimbusRomNo9L-Regu" 0.0130 nil nil 17 "WSWLVM+NimbusRomNo9L-Regu" nil)
  ("tone, content, and style of PLAI is therefore designed with “the other 90%” in mind: the 90% of students" 0.12095 0.90422 0.36805 0.37964 0.37908 0.01158 0.00564 0.2965 0.0361 "WSWLVM+NimbusRomNo9L-Regu" 0.0130 nil nil 18 "WSWLVM+NimbusRomNo9L-Regu" nil)
  ("who will never take an advanced languages class, and yet a few of whom may go on to create languages." 0.12095 0.88709 0.38415 0.39573 0.39573 0.01158 0.00458 0.3074 0.0316 "WSWLVM+NimbusRomNo9L-Regu" 0.0130 nil nil 19 "WSWLVM+NimbusRomNo9L-Regu" nil)
  ("This also has implications for content. For instance, the majority of students have their heads filled" 0.14104 0.90421 0.40024 0.41182 0.41182 0.01158 0.00729 0.2464 0.0326 "WSWLVM+NimbusRomNo9L-Regu" 0.0130 nil nil 15 "WSWLVM+NimbusRomNo9L-Regu" nil)
  ("with half-truths and falsehoods about garbage collection. In many departments, the PL course is the only" 0.12095 0.90421 0.41633 0.42792 0.42736 0.01158 0.00586 0.2592 0.0326 "WSWLVM+NimbusRomNo9L-Regu" 0.0130 nil nil 15 "WSWLVM+NimbusRomNo9L-Regu" nil)
  ("place to correct these. That means the course should confront these misconceptions by comparing garbage" 0.12095 0.90421 0.43243 0.44401 0.44401 0.01158 0.00495 0.2724 0.0387 "WSWLVM+NimbusRomNo9L-Regu" 0.0130 nil nil 14 "WSWLVM+NimbusRomNo9L-Regu" nil)
  ("collection to manual memory management. I also find that having students implement a collector or two" 0.12095 0.90421 0.44852 0.46011 0.46011 0.01158 0.00594 0.3147 0.0723 "WSWLVM+NimbusRomNo9L-Regu" 0.0130 nil nil 15 "WSWLVM+NimbusRomNo9L-Regu" nil)
