  ("designers must wed the demands of the domain to general-purpose notions (abstraction, iteration, etc.)." 0.12095 0.87577 0.62876 0.64034 0.64034 0.01158 0.00458 0.3045 0.0692 "WSWLVM+NimbusRomNo9L-Regu" 0.0130 nil nil 13 "WSWLVM+NimbusRomNo9L-Regu" nil)
  ("As a design guideline, throughout the semester students re-examine the implications of the Scheme" 0.14104 0.90421 0.64485 0.65644 0.65644 0.01158 0.0074 0.2646 0.0204 "WSWLVM+NimbusRomNo9L-Regu" 0.0130 nil nil 13 "WSWLVM+NimbusRomNo9L-Regu" nil)
  ("report’s dictum, “Programming languages should be designed not by piling feature on top of feature, but" 0.12095 0.90421 0.66095 0.67253 0.67253 0.01158 0.00583 0.2642 0.0560 "WSWLVM+NimbusRomNo9L-Regu" 0.0130 nil nil 15 "WSWLVM+NimbusRomNo9L-Regu" nil)
